Elastic IP (EIP)
-----------------
An Elastic IP (EIP) is a static public IPv4 address in Amazon Web Services (AWS).

Unlike a normal public IP that may change when an EC2 instance is stopped and started, an Elastic IP remains yours until you release it. 
You can associate it with an EC2 instance or network interface and quickly remap it to another resource if needed.

A common setup is:

Internet → Elastic IP → EC2 instance

AWS generally charges for public IPv4 addresses, including Elastic IPs, so you typically want to allocate only what you need.

